# UX: how {{NAME}} behaves

Read this before building any screen, together with the screen's file in `{{DOCS_DIR}}/prototype/screens/`. It is written
from the product interview (create) or from the existing screens, confirmed with the owner (extract); `/plumb:ux` reviews
built screens against it. Replace the prompts below with this product's real answers.

{{DEFAULTS_NOTE}}

## Users and context

Who: {{AUDIENCE}}.
What the product is: {{DESCRIPTION}}
Where and how they use it (device, place, interruptions, how often): _to fill_.

## Key tasks and flows

List each task as: who, goal, start, steps, end, and the screens it crosses. Name the one task that must be fastest.

## Navigation

The navigation model (sidebar, top bar, bottom tabs, deep links), what is always reachable, how a user gets back, what
changes between narrow and wide screens.

## Page anatomy

The templates the screens are built from (list, detail, form, dashboard, settings): header, primary action, content, secondary
panel, footer. One primary action per view.

## Forms

Labels above fields; required fields marked in words; validate on blur and on submit, never on the first keystroke; errors say
what is wrong and how to fix it, next to the field and in a summary; keep what the user typed; confirm before losing work.

## States (every screen has all that apply)

| State | What the user sees |
|---|---|
| Loading | Skeleton in the final layout; no spinner wall. |
| Empty | What is missing, why, one action. |
| Error | What happened in words, what to do, retry. |
| Success | A clear confirmation; where the user goes next. |
| Disabled | Still readable; says why when it is not obvious. |
| Long text | Wraps or truncates with the full text available. |
| Zero and one | Counts and plurals read correctly. |
| Offline | What still works, what does not, when it syncs. |

## Feedback and confirmation

Immediate feedback for every action; toasts confirm what happened; undo beats "are you sure" for reversible actions.
Destructive actions name the thing, say what is lost and use the `danger` variant, on a confirmation only.

## Onboarding and first run

What a new user sees first, how long until they have done something useful, what is skippable.

## Voice and microcopy

Voice: {{VOICE}}. Words for statuses, actions, durations and dates are fixed in [vocabulary.md](vocabulary.md). Sentence case,
plain words, no exclamation marks, no blame in errors.

